  abstract = {A correlation-energy formula due to Colle and Salvetti [Theor. Chim. Acta 3'7, 329 (1975)],in which the correlation energy density is expressed in terms of the electron density and a Laplacian of the second-order Hartree-Fock density matrix, is restated as a formula involving the density and local kinetic-energy density. On insertion of gradient expansions for the 1ocal kinetic-energy density, density-functional formulas for the correlation energy and correlation potential are then obtained. Through numerical calculations on a number of atoms, positive ions, and molecules, of both open- and closed-shell type, it is demonstrated that these formulas, like the original Colle- Salvetti formulas, give correlation energies within a few percent.},
  langid = {english},
