  abstract = {This chapter presents a simplified and nonmathematical description of the molecular orbital (MO) theory as a background aid for understanding the pericyclic mechanisms. The emphasis is on the pictorial description of MOs, particularly pi MOs in terms of H{\"u}ckel theory and on their properties with reference to orbital symmetry, energies and coefficients. The perturbation effects of different types of substituents on the frontier orbital energies and coefficients of pi systems are described. The pi MOs of trimethylenemethane and fulvene systems are included. The cyclic conjugated pi systems in terms of H{\"u}ckel and M{\"o}bius systems and the concept of aromaticity and antiaromaticity in these systems are also described.},
