  urldate = {2023-08-31},
  abstract = {A hydrocarbon is an organic chemical compound composed exclusively of hydrogen and carbon atoms. Hydrocarbon molecules naturally occur and are found in crude oil, natural gas, coal, and other important sources of energy. Burning hydrocarbon derivatives in the presence of sufficient oxygen produces carbon dioxide, water, and heat, which is why hydrocarbon derivatives are desirable as fuels. This chapter presents the various sources of hydrocarbons including the conventional sources, such as crude oil and natural gas, and the unconventional sources, such as tar sand bitumen, coal, oil shale, and biomass.},
